WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:07.600 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  thank you very much and it's a great  pleasure and honor that I've been  invited here tonight there is a famous  famous Jewish saying that words should  be weighed not counted there are no  speeches that we can give no words of  comfort or solace we can offer that can  never take away the pain of what  happened in hallow on Yom Kippur  today we honor those young victims who  got killed while simply living their  lives in front of the local synagogue we  stand together with our families and  their loved ones as they go through  trauma which no one should ever have to  we thank the heroes who protected others  who showed us that faced with evil  humanity is capable of good but today we  cannot help thinking of the fear the  fear of all the victims and witnesses  like you Anastacia  the fear of the Jewish congregation  inside the synagogue and we think of the  fear that every Jewish person in Europe  felt in that moment that heart-sinking  fear that Europe's Jewish community  knows all too well that fear which comes  back stronger after every anti-semitic  attack that is reported on the news from  the Brussels meeting you Jewish Museum  we just saw in the film - the kosher  supermarket in Paris from the Jewish  school in Toulouse to the synagogue in  hallow and in the last days alone we  have seen Bobby beaten up on the streets  of London  and the Jewish cemeteries vandalized in  via time for every one of those  incidents we see in the news there are  many more which happen every single day  across our Union they may be smaller and  less violent in nature but they are real  and they are on the rise and they create  an atmosphere in which Jews no longer  feel safe and start doubting the future  in Europe ladies and gentlemen these  attacks because small our attacks on the  Jewish community but their consequences  and their repercussions are attacks on  all of us on our way of life our values  of Tolerance our unity in diversity  anti-semitism is a poison for our  community and it is up to all to fight  it to prevent it and to eradicate it the  fight against anti-semitism is as much  for every other part of our community as  it is for Jewish people and it is one  which must be led at local regional  national and European level we must all  do our part the Jewish community is not  alone this is the message I will take  with me to Yad Vashem in Jerusalem in  January we will lead this fight together  we will build on the work done in the  last years in the Commission in the  Parliament and in the Member States but  as rising challenge needs a stronger  response from outside indeed as you  mentioned I haven't  that my vice pretty the president  margaritas kinas to lead the fight  against anti-semitism and today I can  announce that he will be supported by a  new dedicated team with very experienced  people who will work with our  coordinator for combating anti-semitism  and for fostering Jewish life and  fostering Jewish life is something which  I've always taken very seriously as  Minister of Defense I decided to  reintroduce after 100 years hobbies as  chaplains in the Bundeswehr the armed  forces together with Christian priests  this is as important for Jewish soldiers  as it is for the rest of the armed  forces it is a way to learn about the  different cultures that together build a  common European culture and it is a way  to understand one another to understand  that in our diversity of backgrounds we  are all part of the same community there  would be no European culture without  Jewish culture and there would be no  Europe without Jewish people we will  remain vigilant and more we will act at  all levels through security means of  course but also in our education system  and in the public debate there is one  fundamental freedom that we Europeans  must reclaim and that is the freedom  from fear whatever they believe in thank  you so much  [Applause]

